{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_3>\nn, m = map(int, input().split())\nvalues = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\nmid = n // 2\nA = values[:mid]\nB = values[mid:]\n\nlenA = len(A)\nlenB = len(B)\n\nlistA = []\nfor mask in range(1 << lenA):\n    acc = 0\n    for idx in range(lenA):\n        if mask & (1 << idx):\n            acc += A[idx]\n    listA.append(acc % m)\n\nlistB = []\nfor mask in range(1 << lenB):\n    acc = 0\n    for idx in range(lenB):\n        if mask & (1 << idx):\n            acc += B[idx]\n    listB.append(acc % m)\n\nlistA.sort()\nlistB.sort()\n\nmax_val = 0\n\ndef upper_bound_search(arr, val):\n    lo, hi = 0, len(arr) - 1\n    best = 0\n    while lo <= hi:\n        mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n        if arr[mid] < val:\n            best = arr[mid]\n            lo = mid + 1\n        else:\n            hi = mid - 1\n    return best\n\nfor x in listA:\n    y_needed = m - x\n    y = upper_bound_search(listB, y_needed)\n    cur = (x + y) % m\n    if cur > max_val:\n        max_val = cur\n\nprint(max_val)\n</your_rewritten_code_3>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint upper_bound_search(vector<int>& arr, int val) {\n    int lo = 0, hi = arr.size() - 1;\n    int best = 0;\n    while (lo <= hi) {\n        int mid = (lo + hi) / 2;\n        if (arr[mid] < val) {\n            best = arr[mid];\n            lo = mid + 1;\n        } else {\n            hi = mid - 1;\n        }\n    }\n    return best;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n, m;\n    cin >> n >> m;\n    \n    vector<int> values(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        cin >> values[i];\n    }\n    \n    int mid = n / 2;\n    vector<int> A(values.begin(), values.begin() + mid);\n    vector<int> B(values.begin() + mid, values.end());\n    \n    int lenA = A.size();\n    int lenB = B.size();\n    \n    vector<int> listA;\n    for (int mask = 0; mask < (1 << lenA); mask++) {\n        int acc = 0;\n        for (int idx = 0; idx < lenA; idx++) {\n            if (mask & (1 << idx)) {\n                acc += A[idx];\n            }\n        }\n        listA.push_back(acc % m);\n    }\n    \n    vector<int> listB;\n    for (int mask = 0; mask < (1 << lenB); mask++) {\n        int acc = 0;\n        for (int idx = 0; idx < lenB; idx++) {\n            if (mask & (1 << idx)) {\n                acc += B[idx];\n            }\n        }\n        listB.push_back(acc % m);\n    }\n    \n    sort(listA.begin(), listA.end());\n    sort(listB.begin(), listB.end());\n    \n    int max_val = 0;\n    \n    for (int x : listA) {\n        int y_needed = m - x;\n        int y = upper_bound_search(listB, y_needed);\n        int cur = (x + y) % m;\n        if (cur > max_val) {\n            max_val = cur;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    cout << max_val << endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00014804698002990335, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -4.768370445